 484| ## 5. SETTLED PREMISES -- re-inlined so nobody spends an answer re-deriving them
 485| 
 486| Copied forward from the pass-1 brief's section 5 (`pass1_20261022/packet.md`), pruned to what a question here depends on,
 487| and appended with what pass 1 (`PASS1_RULINGS.md` A/B as amended by E; `CHECKS_mainloop.md`) and the build
 488| (`table1_20261022/`) settled.  **Each was RE-READ IN THIS SCOPE** -- the working tree over HEAD `5986c137` -- by the
 489| drafter; line numbers are the working tree's.  `cpu_m88k_instr.c`, `cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c`, `cpu_dyntrans.c`,
 490| `cpu_m88k.c`, `Makefile.skel`, `regress/lib.sh` and `regress/run.sh` are byte-identical to HEAD; in the generator every
 491| line before 254 is unchanged and every line after it moved by +4.
 492| 
 493| * **S1 -- the generation early return is KEPT.**  `loadstore()` still returns on `if (size == 0 && scaledness)`
 494|   (generator :104-105; the diff does not touch it), so no handler is generated for a scaled byte and no name with
 495|   `_scaled` exists for size 0.  (A2.)
 496| * **S2 -- the deleted arm and its three siblings.**  HEAD's table printer had four `NULL` arms: `store && signedness`
 497|   (:239-242), `!registeroffset && usr` (:244-247), `!registeroffset && scaledness` (:249-252) -- all three unchanged -- and
 498|   `size == 0 && scaledness` (HEAD :254-257), which the diff deletes whole.  MEASURED: 296 `NULL` of 512 at HEAD
 499|   (BASELINE.out section 4), split 128 + 96 + 48 + 24 by arm (the pass-1 census, `pass1_20261022/packet.md` section 7;
 500|   PRETABLE.out section 1); 272 after the fix (FIX.out; the drafter's re-parse, S18a).
 501| * **S3 -- the consumers, unchanged by the diff (cpu_m88k_instr.c; section 8.2).**  `X(xmem_slow)` indexes
 502|   `m88k_loadstore[...]` for its load half (:2377-2382) and its store half (:2411-2417), ALWAYS adding
 503|   `M88K_LOADSTORE_NO_PC_SYNC` and NEVER `M88K_LOADSTORE_SIGNEDNESS`, takes `scaled` from `iword & 0x200` (:2357) and
 504|   `user` from `iword & 0x80` (:2359), and calls both slots with no NULL test (:2395, :2426).  The register-form `ld`/`st`
 505|   decoder installs `m88k_loadstore[...]` as `ic->f` (:3622-3629: adds SCALEDNESS and USR, never NO_PC_SYNC), and a NULL
 506|   `ic->f` reaches `fatal("INTERNAL ERROR: ic->f == NULL!\n"); goto bad;` (cpu_dyntrans.c:1906-1908), which stops the
 507|   emulated CPU.  The immediate form (:3087-3091) never adds SCALEDNESS, USR or REGISTEROFFSET.  Exactly these four
 508|   sites index the table (CHECKS #3).
