 519|   0, 1, 2, or 3 bits (multiplied by scale factor 1, 2, 4, or 8) for byte, half-word, word, or double-word accesses,
 520|   respectively. For byte accesses, the 5UBOPCODE [OCR for SUBOPCODE] field is distinctly different from the register
 521|   indirect with index (unscaled) cases but the result is identical."  The handlers compute
 522|   `reg(ic->arg[1]) + LS_SIZE * reg(ic->arg[2])` under `LS_SCALED` (cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:65-70 generic, :248-253
 523|   fast), `LS_SIZE` 1 for a byte.  `print_function_name()` appends `_scaled` only `if (scaledness && size > 0)` (:80-81)
 524|   and prints `_le` for EVERY byte entry whatever its endianness (:74-75), so each repaired slot prints its index-32
