  20| 
  21|   so the driver compiles with the compiler the gate detected (cc or gcc).  A host with no compiler then SKIPS GATE 2 at
  22|   `:184` as before this round, the way every other differential in the gate does; a host WITH a compiler still gets a
  23|   RED row (never a skip) for a missing generator/table, a failed compile, a failed run (B5 unchanged).
  24| * The block's comment gains one sentence: "Placed after the gate's compiler detection so the driver gets `$CC`;
  25|   standalone it falls back to cc, then gcc."
